{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27775,"name":"Pham Tan Thinh","username":"ptt2908","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/ptt2908/{size}/12119_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-24T00:37:29.900Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWhat happens to a reusable package as it moves through borrowing, return, and reuse—and what can CKB actually verify about that journey? \u003cstrong\u003eReuseLoop\u003c/strong\u003e is a CKB Testnet prototype that records an item’s administrator-authorized state changes: AVAILABLE → BORROWED → RETURNED → AVAILABLE.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCKB records application state and authorized transitions. Physical handoffs, returns, cleaning, and inspections happen off-chain and are not proven by the chain.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-workflow-overview-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-workflow-overview-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWorkflow overview\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe diagram separates the current read-only walkthrough from the lifecycle modeled by the prototype.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"mermaid\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-mermaid\"\u003eflowchart TD\n  subgraph Demo[\"Current walkthrough: read-only\"]\n    Item[\"Existing CKB Testnet item\"] --\u0026gt; Read[\"ReuseLoop reads item state and confirmed history\"]\n    Read --\u0026gt; View[\"Operator sees current status and available action\"]\n  end\n\n  subgraph Lifecycle[\"Lifecycle represented\"]\n    Available[\"AVAILABLE\"] --\u0026gt;|Borrow| Borrowed[\"BORROWED\"]\n    Borrowed --\u0026gt;|Confirm return| Returned[\"RETURNED\"]\n    Returned --\u0026gt;|Make available| Available\n  end\n\n  Physical[\"Handoff, return, cleaning, inspection\"] -.-\u0026gt; Offchain[\"Off-chain events are not proven by CKB state\"]\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-how-the-transaction-path-works-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-how-the-transaction-path-works-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow the transaction path works\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn operator selects an allowed state transition and reviews its preview. One configured administrator approves it in JoyID. The app submits the signed transaction to CKB Testnet, tracks confirmation, then refreshes the item state and history.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe current walkthrough is read-only: it reuses an existing Registry and item and submits no new lifecycle transaction. CKB Lock Scripts verify the administrator’s signature; Type Scripts enforce Registry membership and valid transitions. The MVP has no separate borrower or store keys and no multi-party authorization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-testnet-evidence-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-testnet-evidence-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eTestnet evidence\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe demo item completed a full lifecycle on CKB Testnet. Each link opens its confirmed transaction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eAction\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eState\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eConfirmed block\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eTransaction\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eItem registered\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAVAILABLE\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e22,999,622\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pudge.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x851d6f428defd2871b0124ea3893249a24a2a30a09970463c4d2953381d71660\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eTransaction\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eBorrow\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eBORROWED\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e22,999,649\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pudge.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0xd88b93213ffcacac9ba691dae189f77c5a631380549246df2a8afb9fa4aa51a1\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eTransaction\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eConfirm return\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRETURNED\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e22,999,692\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pudge.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x3ac18f18c7831e44c369bae00282255adbfaa7f7b05e3bb572d062e0e5be2a1c\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eTransaction\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eMake available\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAVAILABLE\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e22,999,731\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pudge.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x71574211cc4a674571b330ca9de6a1beb4215971d2e9911369e9e4865137a482\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eTransaction\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-repository-and-walkthrough-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-repository-and-walkthrough-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRepository and walkthrough\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ptt2908/ReuseLoop\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub repository\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ptt2908/ReuseLoop/blob/main/docs/week12-demo.md\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRead-only Testnet walkthrough\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe app currently runs locally; the project documentation does not list a hosted demo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-verification-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-verification-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVerification\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn 24 November 2026, the application suite passed all 62 tests across 9 files, and the production build succeeded. The minified JavaScript bundle is 799.26 kB (250.05 kB gzipped), above Vite’s 500 kB warning threshold. npm run lint currently reports three errors: synchronous state updates inside an effect in ItemLifecyclePanel.tsx and an unused err variable in ItemLookupPanel.tsx.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Rust contract suite passed all 77 tests with no failures on 24 November 2026 (99.43 seconds). The make test helper still reports a Clang version detection warning; this run does not verify a fresh RISC-V binary build or its hash. Browser-level JoyID and RPC failure tests remain outstanding.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27775-feedback-welcome-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27775-feedback-welcome-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeedback welcome\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs a single configured administrator a reasonable authorization model for this MVP? Which roles should be added next?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs the distinction clear between on-chain state transitions and off-chain physical handling?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich failure cases, setup friction, or UX gaps should we address next?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks for taking a look. I would especially value feedback on the authorization model and on how to represent physical events without overstating what the chain proves.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-11-24T00:37:29.900Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":14,"readers_count":13,"score":42.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":11356,"topic_slug":"reuseloop-tracking-reusable-packaging-lifecycles-on-ckb-testnet","display_username":"Pham Tan Thinh","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recove